+/* One NAPI poll per queue.
+ *
+ * This must not exceed NAPI_POLL_WEIGHT (64): netif_napi_add_weight() emits
+ * "called with weight %d" via netdev_err_once() for anything larger, and no
+ * in-tree driver does it. A larger weight is also pointless here, because
+ * net_rx_action() bounds a poll round by netdev_budget (300 packets) and
+ * netdev_budget_usecs (2 ms) regardless of the per-NAPI weight, so raising
+ * the weight past 64 cannot increase the work done per softirq round -- it
+ * only makes a single queue able to starve its siblings within one round.
+ *
+ * With 8 RSS queues at 2.5G/64B each ring sees ~465 kpps, so weight 64 costs
+ * ~7.3k NAPI exits/s per queue, about 1.5% of one P-core. See
+ * audit/00_design_space.md section 6.
+ */
+#define R8169_NAPI_WEIGHT	NAPI_POLL_WEIGHT
